INTERPRETATION (R35):
- BRACKET: floor (naive/loramerge ~0.37-0.39) < EWC/continued (~0.46) < ours (0.890) < oracle (0.994).
- EWC (a real anti-forgetting regularizer) beats naive (0.456 vs 0.390) but is CRUSHED by replay
  (0.890): regularization-only is NOT sufficient to replace rehearsal; EWC still shows an age gradient.
  => replay-consolidation's dominance over standard CL is not an artifact of weak baselines.
- ORACLE_GAP +0.10 seen / +0.16 para: no-gold self-distill replay is close to but NOT within the
  0.03-0.05 "essentially matched" band of the gold-old upper bound. Honest reading: having old gold
  still buys ~0.10-0.16; the no-gold approximation's bottleneck is scaffold/teacher answer quality and
  self-distill snapshot fidelity, not the replay principle. Improving the scaffold guard / replay
  sampling is the lever to close it. This does NOT overturn R33 (ours still dominates all rehearsal-free
  and regularizer baselines and needs no gold/no inference memory), it sharpens where the headroom is.

BOTTOM LINE: R35 closes the replay-consolidation chapter's brackets — ours sits well above every
rehearsal-free / regularizer baseline and within ~0.10 of the gold-old ceiling. The remaining open
problem is rehearsal-FREE continual learning (no replay at all), which R36-I attacks. Pod terminated.
